# Locators and waits

## Locators, in order of preference

1. `getByRole(role, { name })`, with `exact: true` when the name is a full label.
2. `getByLabel`, `getByText` for visible text the ticket talks about.
3. Stable app class names already in use (`.nxl-*`, `.billing-*`, `.rbc-event`, `.ant-select-*`) when there is no accessible name.
4. Never XPath or nth-child chains, except to reach a control that has no label (comment why).

Scope to the dialog or row first (`page.getByRole('dialog').last()`, `page.locator('tr').filter({ hasText: id })`),
then find controls inside it.

## Waiting

- Prefer web-first assertions (`await expect(locator).toBeVisible()`) and `locator.waitFor(...)`.
- `page.waitForTimeout` only to let a debounced search or a save settle, never above ~1.5s, and never as the
  only wait for something you then assert.
- Optional UI (a control that only some builds show): `if (await x.isVisible().catch(() => false)) ...`.
  Do not use this pattern for something the ticket requires; let it fail instead.
- Loading splashes are handled by `waitForShell` / `gotoPortal` / `readPage`. Do not re-implement them.

## Timeouts

Config defaults: test 360s, expect and actions 25s, navigation 45s. Override per call only when a step is known
to be slower (email delivery, calendar load), and put the reason in the step name or a short comment.
